<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The vocabularies that live in `:core:` and therefore cannot hold a resource
  id: routes, substance categories, interaction severities, combination
  severities, tolerance classes and their effect axes.

  Those modules are plain JVM and carry no Android resources on purpose — it is
  what lets the pharmacology be tested in milliseconds — so the English label
  stays there as a fallback and the localized label lives here, resolved at the
  point of drawing. `ui/labels/CoreLabels.kt` is the only thing that should read
  these; a screen that reaches for `route.displayName`, or that prints a
  `wireValue`, is showing English to a Chinese reader.

  Exception, and the reason this file has no `binding_*` entries: `BindingAction`
  and `BindingAffinity` are resolved through `shell_binding_*` in
  `strings_shell.xml`, which is where they already lived and were already
  translated. See `CoreLabels`' KDoc for why they were not moved.
-->
